            <key>reason</key>
            <string>The lowercase phonetic source bearings caused actual repeated-ink intersections in six cuts. Native y.sc itself has negative pair margins in heavier cuts, so it does not close the observed issue. Use the native w.sc outer-edge frame, retaining genuine italic overhang and a positive repeated pair gap without changing the drawing.</string>
